EasyScript interactive shell. Type a sentence, like: say "hello"
End a line with ":" to start a block (an if, a loop, or a function); a blank line ends it.
Lines with errors aren't kept. Type exit to leave.
>> >> ... ... ... two
still two
>> ... ... 1
2
>> ... ... >> 42
>> ... ... (That block wasn't kept.)
>> after the bad block
>> 